  "independent_evidence": "Assumptions (stated to the model in the Stage B task block): the supplied tree ((a,b)x,c)r and supplied cognate units are correct; within one cognate unit, gain and loss of a segment or piece cost one event each on a branch (unweighted parsimony); c's g corresponds to k. Material present in exactly one of a/b is present at x when c shows it in the same unit (one loss beats two gains) and absent when c's same-unit form lacks it (one gain beats two losses). With no c form the two histories tie. Values at x come from the daughter that has them. Counterbalancing: a ends every core in k (retained or added), b never does, and vowels, onsets and stem shapes are balanced across retain and absent items, so no visible cue other than c predicts the answer.",
